# Git identity — visify-apps only

For this repository (and any Visify Apps work):

- **Author name:** `visify-apps`
- **Author email:** `visifyapps@gmail.com`
- **GitHub account:** `visify-apps`

Never commit or push as any other name or email (including personal accounts, Cursor agent defaults, or company emails).

When creating commits, set identity via environment variables for that command only (do **not** change global/local `git config` unless the user explicitly asks):

```bash
GIT_AUTHOR_NAME="visify-apps" \
GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL="visifyapps@gmail.com" \
GIT_COMMITTER_NAME="visify-apps" \
GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL="visifyapps@gmail.com" \
git commit ...
```

If a commit was created with the wrong identity, rewrite/amend it to `visify-apps <visifyapps@gmail.com>` before pushing.
